# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# ── APEX TO WWW ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every canonical URL this site publishes — in <link rel="canonical">,
# in sitemap.xml, in hreflang, in every printed volume — is on the www
# host. If the apex also serves the site, the same page exists at two
# addresses, which splits how search engines see it and makes any
# cookie or origin-scoped setting ambiguous.
#
# This rule only takes effect once worldwencollege.co.uk (the apex) is
# attached to this Pages project as a custom domain. If the apex is
# instead pointed elsewhere, or not configured at all, the rule is inert
# — it costs nothing and starts working the moment the domain is added.
# Nothing here can break the www host, which is what serves the site
# today.
# TODO(domain): the College's former-name apex. When an Albalagh domain
# is registered this rule moves to it — and this one STAYS, redirecting
# the old host rather than retiring it, because every credential and
# printed volume issued so far names it. docs/domain-setup.md § Pending.
https://worldwencollege.co.uk/*  https://www.worldwencollege.co.uk/:splat  301!

# ── HTML EXTENSIONS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The build writes directory-style paths (/about/, not /about.html). A
# visitor arriving from an old link, a printed document or a mistyped
# address should land on the page rather than a 404.
/index.html      /            301
/about.html      /about/      301
/academics.html  /academics/  301
/admissions.html /admissions/ 301
/faculty.html    /faculty/    301
/contact.html    /contact/    301
/faq.html        /faq/        301

# ── SECTION SHORTHANDS ───────────────────────────────────────────────
